Hello hello! I've made this logbook to hopefully answer any questions that arise from reading the code in this repository. It should do so but providing a "versioned" log of my thoughts and opinions of what this service should look like. This would usually not be committed, but I think it'll be useful here ;)

- Tech debt, and other things that engineers need to do but don't provide any lingering value (think Q1 or Q3 quadrants in the Eisenhower matrix)
- Needs to expose some sort of endpoint to provide statistics on the runs for each issue (1 issue may have many runs..)
    - MCP endpoint for a local LLM to query statistics (not MVP)
- Technically, this could all be made possible with a slack message to Devin with the issue number, but that makes centralised statistics, self-governance and ownership more difficult.
- Let's use a hardcoded Devin client so that Devin is the default option for running runs (although in theory any agent could satisfy an abstraction of what Devin provides.)